{"at": "2026-11-19T19:46:10Z", "class": ["owner-preference"], "evidence": ["owner:turn@2026-11-19T19:37:50.864Z#cb3bdcdf49d4"], "id": "a61de02e4d7160c0", "kind": "note", "scope": "global", "session": "ddb4ef0a-ba7d-5ef4-8aa5-b4cb3d5afff8", "signal": "owner-correction", "text": "Reply to the owner first and at once, every time a message arrives: acknowledge, then do or answer what he asked before returning to earlier work. Keep long jobs (sweeps, browser passes, release gates) in the background so they are neither stopped by his message nor make him wait. Never hold the conversation with a long foreground wait.", "trust": "owner-stated"}
{"at": "2026-11-19T20:02:45Z", "class": ["data-pipeline"], "evidence": ["gate:check passed after the fix; nine closed postings had returned in release a093eb1"], "id": "ad6102b4d9bab42f", "kind": "note", "scope": "global", "session": "ddb4ef0a-ba7d-5ef4-8aa5-b4cb3d5afff8", "signal": "rework", "text": "A check that visits only what is currently listed lets removed items come back: once a closed posting left the list, the open-or-closed check stopped visiting it, its record vanished, and the next rebuild listed it again. Whatever a check removes must stay among its targets (or its verdict must be carried over), and two rebuilds in a row must give the same list.", "trust": "observed"}
{"at": "2026-11-19T20:02:45Z", "class": ["verification"], "evidence": ["gate:check failed on the first run of the new page (fact check), passed after titles were quoted"], "id": "7b09bf8022a85dc0", "kind": "note", "scope": "global", "session": "ddb4ef0a-ba7d-5ef4-8aa5-b4cb3d5afff8", "signal": "rework", "text": "Run the project's whole gate on a newly generated page before calling it complete, not only the page's own checker: here the project's fact check read titles such as 'I Hate Job Interviews' as first-person claims, which the page's own check could not know.", "trust": "observed"}
